---
# ansible-lint configuration. Like ansible.cfg, this is read from the working
# directory, so every ansible-lint run happens from here: cd ansible/
#
# The profile is written down rather than inherited. ansible-lint ships a
# ladder of profiles — min, basic, moderate, safety, shared, production — and
# without this line it grades the repository against them and reports which one
# it reached, failing only on error-level rules. Naming `production` turns that
# report into a gate: anything short of the top profile fails the build.
#
# This is set to the strictest rung because the playbooks and the role already
# pass it clean, so it costs nothing today and catches the first task that
# would have slipped below it. Adopting a standard while you already meet it is
# free; adopting one after you have drifted is a refactor.
profile: production
